# ICPS2023_5 experimental 1M OpenRCX model. This is intentionally partial.
# OpenRCX's per-distance resistance table uses ohms per nanometre. The sheet
# values are from libs.tech/klayout/pex/icps2023_5_pex.py: POLY is the one
# exception, taken from the local experimental router tech LEF (25 ohm/sq).
#
# No metal wire capacitance, coupling, fringe, field-solver, or PEX return-path
# term is qualified here. PEX's 0.086 fF/um^2 term belongs to NAREA/PAREA
# diffusion-to-SUB, not POLY/TiN/ML1 interconnect. Do not use this as signoff.
# PEX contact references per 25 um^2: Al-TiN 0.9 ohm, Al-N+ 150 ohm, and
# Al-P+ 200 ohm. CAP_TO_SUB is 0.086 fF/um^2 for both N/P diffusion; it is
# not a metal-wire term and is deliberately not mapped onto routing layers.

#
# The VIA_TIN_M1 entry converts the PEX Al-TiN contact (0.9 ohm for 5x5 um)
# through R_A=0.9*25=22.5 ohm*um^2 to the local 0.08x0.08 um experimental
# cut: R=22.5/0.0064=3515.625 ohm. This is an explicit inverse-area
# extrapolation, not a measured 0.08 um contact.

Extraction Rules for OpenRCX
Version 1.2
DIAGMODEL OFF
LayerCount 3
DensityRate 1 0
Corners 1 : nom_xyce_3v_25c
DensityModel 0

Metal 1 RESOVER
WIDTH Table 1 entries: 0.12
Metal 1 RESOVER 0
DIST count 1 width 0.12
0.20 0.20 0 0 0.208333333333
END DIST

Metal 2 RESOVER
WIDTH Table 1 entries: 0.14
Metal 2 RESOVER 0
DIST count 1 width 0.14
0.14 0.14 0 0 0.142857142857
END DIST

Metal 3 RESOVER
WIDTH Table 1 entries: 6.0
Metal 3 RESOVER 0
DIST count 1 width 6.0
4.0 4.0 0 0 0.0000333333333333
END DIST

VIARES 1 Default LEF Vias:
3515.625 VIA_TIN_M1 cuts 1 TopMetal 3 BotMetal 2 dx 80 dy 80
END VIARES

END DensityModel 0
